erts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed; beginning held-out TDD in worktree janitor-aa9e-3d35.","timestamp":1788469034333024001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"BLOCKED before RED: docs/security.md is fully generated by scripts/gen_config_reference.py ('do not edit by hand'; drift test under make test enforces this). The ticket AC requires adding scanner-lock/update/recovery content to docs/security.md, but the generator that owns that file is outside declared file_impact. Per leaf protocol, stopping rather than editing outside scope.","timestamp":1788469088111957001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SCOPE CORRECTION (orchestrator): docs/security.md is FULLY GENERATED by\nscripts/gen_config_reference.py (carries a \"do not edit by hand\" banner; a drift test under\nmake test fails if stale). The generator already has a \"Curated narrative (security.md) — NOT\nregistry-derivable\" region (gen_config_reference.py:103), which is exactly where the AC's\nscanner-lock authority/checksum-provenance/bump/recovery procedure belongs. Added\nscripts/gen_config_reference.py + its drift tests (test_gen_config_reference.py,\ntest_generated_surface_markers.py) to file_impact; docs/security.md stays as the regenerated\noutput. Edit the generator's curated narrative and regenerate — do NOT hand-edit security.md. No\nother Wave-1 agent touches these files.","timestamp":1788469180510618647},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Revised plan after scope correction: docs/security.md content will be authored in scripts/gen_config_reference.py's curated security narrative, with generator-level docs oracle and drift-check proof before implementation.","timestamp":1788469791820384001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented pinned review scanner contracts in worktree janitor-aa9e-3d35. RED held-out oracle captured missing generated security docs, lock manifest, installer fallback/integrity, and workflow/vote wiring; GREEN after implementation; mutation killed by removing Gerrit scanner success requirement. Local gates: held-out+targeted 107 passed, lint/typecheck passed, scanner lock validation passed, scanner target rejects unsupported macOS host as expected. Full make test hit pre-existing lifecycle failure also reproduced on clean origin/main baseline.","timestamp":1788475914532693001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"BLOCKED after Gerrit CI: change 2595 failed Verified on repository contract tests that require edits outside corrected file_impact: tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py (vote.needs route coverage), tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py (locked workflow-name table), and .github/mechanism-baseline.json or equivalent mechanism-baseline update path for new admitted scanner CI gates. Per leaf protocol, stopping rather than editing outside scope; Gerrit change marked WIP.","timestamp":1788478041211358001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 3 pushed to Gerrit change 2595 after fixing LLM advisory correctness in the scanner installer CLI: --install-dir is now honored consistently for install/check/PATH reporting, and --semgrep-venv is passed through to the semgrep installer. Added unit coverage for those CLI paths and the gitleaks archive-without-binary guard. Evidence before push: scanner-focused targeted suite + held-out oracle 176 passed; validate-locks and generated docs check passed; make lint passed; make typecheck passed. Full sanitized make test is still running locally per operator-provided host override while CI gates patch set 3.","timestamp":1788488314118206514},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 4 pushed to Gerrit change 2595. Addressed remaining LLM advisory issues within scope: --check-only without a local archive now verifies installed scanner binaries using the selected prefix; gitleaks archive extraction now streams the named binary into the destination path instead of tar.extract metadata/path handling; added observable tests for check-only dispatch and nested-archive path stripping; replaced the workflow prose-substring assertion with a structural runs-on assertion. Evidence before push: targeted + held-out oracle 178 passed; make lint passed; make typecheck passed.","timestamp":1788490644694452322},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2595 landed after green gates. Patch set 4 labels: LLM-Review +1 at 2026-09-04 03:27:22 UTC; Verified +1 at 2026-09-04 03:36:35 UTC from run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33831682168. Submitted successfully; Gerrit returned status MERGED for Change-Id I38dfbc1ae144642f52c86240941e3a19e87ae5eb. Residual advisory disposition: accepted for this leaf because LLM marked non-blocking and CI verified the strict pinned scanner contract; docs use checksums_url as provenance, not a runtime fetch; download timeout/scheme hardening and extra manifest-negative tests are improvement follow-ups rather than blockers for the hash-locked Verified lane.","timestamp":1788493028455907180},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"REOPENED — this ticket's landed change (6125c534) was REVERTED via Gerrit 2616 (owned by incident ticket 90c7-c465-4037-42d5).\n\nWhat went wrong: 6125c534 merged on a VACUOUS Verified vote. The Verified workflow runs from trusted main via workflow_dispatch, so the newly-added required scanner-integration job never executed on the very change that introduced it — its native-scanner contracts (pytest SCANNER_INTEGRATION_NODES) were never actually run in CI. Once downstream changes did run it (after the dash `set -euo pipefail` portability bug was fixed in 6b034b9f8224), the contract step failed on every change, turning scanner-integration into a red required gate that blocked ALL merges.\n\nRedo guidance when this is picked up again: do NOT re-add a required scanner job until the vacuous-vote escape is closed (tracked in b973 / clubbable-teriyaki-oriole) — a newly-added required CI job must be proven to execute on its own introducing change, and its contracts must pass in CI, before its Verified vote can be trusted. Linking blocked_by b973.","timestamp":1788506614556578592},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Rescoped from the reverted CL 2612 plan to the ADR 0114-compliant re-land: recreate the scanner artifacts, but wire Gerrit scanner-integration as advisory/non-voting and outside the Verified aggregate. Keeping the recorded 18-path file_impact unless implementation proves it must diverge.","timestamp":1788584410167881001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed after plan-review PASS; beginning scanner re-land implementation in worktree janitor-aa9e-scanner.","timestamp":1788585269022308001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788311614552960001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d9c746a6-7c13-4418-aa30-5801810cf136","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"},{"link_uuid":"ba86ab14-fa57-4e2a-bec9-197bad6654e8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"aa9d-3f7a-71d6-41d3"},{"link_uuid":"fafa833e-d404-4f28-a0f3-81fceeb21e62","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2cfb-f6cf-dcb7-424a"},{"link_uuid":"0729a141-54c0-441a-b240-f6b4897bb6bd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9317-fd35-a180-4083"},{"link_uuid":"59d40695-d0f9-4a34-9112-4a6ce60c1c09","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8495-71a1-c4b4-4b49"},{"link_uuid":"68f5bc9d-6507-4156-94b5-d09cd8b5f704","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d82c-decc-5e88-4bb4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThis story re-lands the scanner integration artifacts that were reverted after Gerrit change 2612. The prior landing wired `scanner-integration` directly into the required `Verified` vote aggregate in `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`; when that lane failed on full-route changes, incident `90c7-c465-4037-42d5` showed the result was a self-referential lock that prevented the repair/revert from earning `Verified +1`.\n\nADR 0114 (`docs/adr/0114-advisory-gate-before-hot-path.md`) now requires any new check that may eventually enter the required `Verified` hot path to run advisory first: non-voting, non-blocking, and outside the aggregate's required `needs`, routing conditions, and any other vote-casting wiring. Promotion into the voting path is explicitly out of scope for this ticket and requires a separate future change after the advisory lane has demonstrated a passing run on `main`.\n\n## Scope\n\nRecreate the reverted scanner artifacts from change 2612 as a starting point, adapting them to current `origin/main` and the post-revert parity guards:\n\n- platform-aware scanner manifest at `infra/compose/review-scanners.lock.json` plus per-platform Semgrep hash locks for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64`;\n- scanner provisioning helper and review-bot Dockerfile integration;\n- a POSIX-`dash`-safe Make target for explicit scanner integration validation;\n- unit/contract tests for manifest selection, checksum/hash rejection, scanner contract execution, workflow wiring, documentation generation, and public exposure;\n- reusable scanner workflow plus mirror-CI and Gerrit exact-patchset advisory wiring;\n- generated `docs/security.md` scanner-lock ownership, update, checksum, and recovery narrative.\n\n## Advisory wiring constraint\n\nThe recreated `scanner-integration` Gerrit job must be advisory only. It may depend on the setup jobs needed to check out/classify the patchset, but it must not be listed in the `vote` job's `needs`, must not be part of the `cast Verified` decision, and must not otherwise affect the required `Verified` aggregate. The `vote` job must remain able to cast `Verified +1/-1` from the existing required lanes even if the advisory scanner lane fails. Do not promote scanner integration into the voting path in this change.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse RED-first held-out TDD for the behavioral/static contract that proves the advisory job is outside `vote.needs` while still present for full-route Gerrit runs. Recreate and adapt the reverted tests for the scanner manifest, installer, generated docs, workflow exposure, and native scanner contracts. Preserve b973 parity: `_scanner-integration.yml` and any local-uses path that reaches it must carry the predates-gate `[ -f … ]` guard, and the Make recipe must avoid bash-only constructs (`set -o pipefail`, `[[ … ]]`, arrays, here-strings, and `${var^}`/`${var,}`).\n\nBefore final gates, rebase onto latest `origin/main`, regenerate docs, and verify `docs/config-reference.md` does not drift unexpectedly from the scanner documentation generator change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The reverted scanner artifacts are recreated and adapted against current `origin/main` without editing outside the recorded 18-path file impact.\n- [ ] `infra/compose/review-scanners.lock.json` has independent `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` scanner entries, each with an exact Gitleaks URL and SHA-256 sourced from the matching release checksums asset.\n- [ ] Each platform entry points to a fully resolved Semgrep requirements lock with the same top-level Semgrep version and all required distribution hashes; the installer uses `pip install --require-hashes`.\n- [ ] The review-bot Docker build selects and validates the `linux/arm64` entry, while the reusable Linux x64 CI lane selects and validates the `linux/amd64` entry.\n- [ ] The installer rejects an unsupported platform, a missing scanner, the wrong Gitleaks version/digest, and invalid Semgrep requirement hashes before running the focused contracts.\n- [ ] Valid selected scanner locks allow the explicit native-binary target to run the real Semgrep/Gitleaks integration contracts, while default local tests and unsupported local platforms preserve skip-with-reason behavior and do not provision scanners.\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` owns a curated scanner-lock security narrative; regenerated `docs/security.md` names the manifest as the update authority, the checksum source, a concrete per-platform bump example, and the withdrawn-asset recovery procedure.\n- [ ] The scanner workflow includes the b973 predates-gate guard and the scanner Make recipe is POSIX-`dash`-safe under `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` and `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`.\n- [ ] The scanner lane is wired as advisory for Gerrit: it is non-voting, non-blocking, outside `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` `vote.needs`, and not used by the required `Verified` aggregate or route decision.\n- [ ] Mirror CI may run the reusable scanner lane for visibility, but Gerrit `Verified` voting remains governed only by the existing required aggregate.\n- [ ] OpenGrep, Docker-image builds, normal `make lint`, and default local tests remain outside scope.\n- [ ] The lane's expected cold-run cost is documented as approximately 1.5-3 runner-minutes without extending the existing 22-23 minute critical path when capacity is available.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/compose/review-scanners.lock.json","reason":"platform-aware Gitleaks integrity + Semgrep lock references"},{"path":"infra/compose/review-scanners.linux-amd64.requirements.txt","reason":"hash-locked Semgrep distributions for Verified"},{"path":"infra/compose/review-scanners.linux-arm64.requirements.txt","reason":"hash-locked Semgrep distributions for the Graviton review-bot"},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot","reason":"select arm64 scanner entry via shared provisioner"},{"path":"scripts/install_review_scanners.py","reason":"shared deploy/CI platform selection + integrity enforcement"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"native-binary scanner integration target"},{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"docs/security.md is generator-owned; add scanner-lock curated-narrative section here (security.md is do-not-edit-by-hand, drift-tested)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"drift test for regenerated security.md"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py","reason":"generated-surface marker test for security.md"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py","reason":"run real pinned rule contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_public_exposure.py","reason":"run real pinned exposure contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py","reason":"run Semgrep and Gitleaks integration contracts"},{"path":".github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml","reason":"reusable mirror/Gerrit scanner lane"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"invoke scanner lane on mirror CI"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"invoke exact-patchset lane and require it in vote aggregation"},{"path":"docs/security.md","reason":"regenerated output carrying the scanner-lock section"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py","reason":"vote.needs route coverage changes: the scanner lane is now required by the Verified vote, so the triage comment's aggregated-check routing must include it (AC: lane required by Verified vote)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py","reason":"locked workflow-name set changes: the new reusable scanner lane adds a workflow name (AC: one parallel reusable lane serves mirror CI and Gerrit patchsets)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1788506574905741854,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","2cfb-f6cf-dcb7-424a"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"],["relates_to","8495-71a1-c4b4-4b49"],["relates_to","9317-fd35-a180-4083"],["relates_to","aa9d-3f7a-71d6-41d3"],["relates_to","d82c-decc-5e88-4bb4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"b8c58219-d20e-4ef7-bbbd-f0180cc7d1e6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","ci","security","rp14"],"ticket_id":"aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee","ticket_type":"story","title":"Re-land review scanner integration as advisory","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2a25e4ef-f2f4-4970-9fdd-349605e05a5e","49427ed7-9e2c-4ab4-8a36-404d9b64ecc9","de16bfd0-130a-4bd8-9471-34cd1fca899b","fad50e9c-56ff-46ea-8da6-b101798b5ee1","e7cc3f6c-eeee-4e5d-b4ea-bd53be2e01e8","846a7ff4-23e8-4e26-81e2-6c016827fb47","68f5bc9d-6507-4156-94b5-d09cd8b5f704","2cd14181-9a0d-47fa-9606-c72442d926e6","261edd6e-b419-4c2e-8732-062ea1323986","4cf17e45-08c0-4929-a2a8-8afb01f177c6","b8c58219-d20e-4ef7-bbbd-f0180cc7d1e6","c073dd37-f4da-4608-96f3-857ce5ecec7c","ebe1f504-f4f2-40a5-abd1-7e2107ed1b93"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788589167475863379,"uuid":"c3aed8ac-8b4d-4779-9bdc-d78588b820f5"}